{{c|{{smaller|''a'', axle; ''b'', journal; ''c'', saddle, by means of which the weight of the car rests on the journal; ''d'', chamber for a lubricating substance, having its lid at ''e''.}}}}
the journal of an axle, as of a carriage-wheel, a railroad-car wheel, etc.; the bushing or metal lining of the hub which forms the rotatory bearing of the axle of a vehicle.—{{smaller|'''Axle-box guides,''' the guides for the brasses of an axle-box.—'''Radial axle-box,''' in a railroad-car, a sliding axle-box, so arranged that, with its fellow, it maintains the axle in a position radial to the curve of the track, however its direction may change.}}

'''axle-clip''' (ak′sl-klip), ''n.'' A clevis or bow which unites some other part of a vehicle to the axle.—{{smaller|'''Axle-clip tie,''' the cross-bar which joins and secures the ends of the bow-clip (which see).}}
